= Pastry Case =

To make the pastry, mix the @plain flour{140%g}(plus extra to sprinkle) and @salt{pinch} in a bowl, and then grate in the @cold butter{85%g}. Rub this into the flour, then stir in just as much @ice cold water{} as needed to bring it together into a dough; it should not be sticky. Alternatively use a food processor. Wrap in clingfilm and chill for at least ~{1%hour}. Preheat the oven to 170°C.

Grease a #23 cm tart tin{} and roll out the pastry on a lightly floured surface until large enough to line the tin. Do so, then line with baking paper and weigh down with #baking beans or dried pulses{}. Bake for about ~{15%minutes} until golden.

= Raspberry Compote =

Meanwhile, make the compote by putting the @raspberries{250%g}(fresh or frozen) into a #small pan{} with the @caster sugar{25%g} and @lemon juice{1%tbsp} and bringing to the boil. Simmer for about ~{12%minutes} until thickened. Allow to cool slightly.

= Frangipane =

To make the frangipane, cream together the @butter{110%g} and @caster sugar{110%g} until fluffy, then beat in the @eggs{2}. Fold in the dry ingredients (@ground almonds{110%g}, @plain flour{25%g}, and @baking powder{0.5%tsp}) and @lemon{0.5}(zest) and a @salt{pinch}.

= Assemble and Bake =

Remove the paper and beans and return the pastry to the oven for a couple of minutes until golden. Spread the compote over the base, and top with the frangipane. Level out and bake for ~{15%minutes}. Add the @flaked almonds{25%g} on top and bake for a further ~{5%minutes} until golden and well risen.